{"ts": 1793977083.1516082, "run_id": "bsa_standards__driver_only__claude-haiku-5-5__r0__eb5dfcc1a485", "source": "agent", "event": "assistant_text", "text": "The BSA standards are prepared in assay_plate wells B1\u2013B3, 100 \u00b5L each, using fresh tips for each transfer.\n\n- **B1 (0 mg/mL):** 100 \u00b5L PBS.\n- **B2 (0.5 mg/mL):** 75 \u00b5L PBS + 25 \u00b5L of the 2 mg/mL BSA standard.\n- **B3 (1.0 mg/mL):** 50 \u00b5L PBS + 50 \u00b5L of the 2 mg/mL BSA standard.\n\nThe reagent volumes drew down as expected: PBS went from 40000 to 39775 \u00b5L (225 \u00b5L used) and BSA standard from 10000 to 9925 \u00b5L (75 \u00b5L used). I did not read the plate.\n\nI batched two dependent steps in the first two transfers (pick-up, aspirate, dispense, drop issued together). They still ran in the correct order and the volumes check out, but I ran the rest one step at a time."}
